an easily duplicate your content to a tea and run your channel for you. It means that you're not standing out and you're going to be fighting an uphill battle because hordes of slop are just going to be released every single day. Thousands of videos that look exactly like yours. You got to have something to separate yourself to differentiate yourself from the crowd. Now, again, this is why I'm using the ranking channels as an example here, just cuz it's easy. But many of them, and I'm sure a lot of you guys who have tried ranking, you just get quote unquote lost or buried in the algorithm. And that's not because necessarily the quality of your video is bad. Although to some extent Cream will rise to the top. But it's because there's nothing about your video that is unique at all. The concept has been done 5,000 times and you're even reusing most of the clips. So people have seen your content already. There's not a unique angle because you're not even commentating over it. and it is something that is easily replicatable and duplicated and copied. Exactly. The exact things that you want to look for in a niche to see if it's quote unquote automatable are the exact things that you want to stay away from if you want to actually make a successful YouTube shorts channel. So, I run everything by myself. And this is coming from somebody who actually has made it to the sort of endgame, right? I'm making a decent amount of money from YouTube. I could potentially hire somebody else and I might experiment with it still. But that's something that comes way way later in the game. not something that you can get into doing, right? If it's your first foray into YouTube and you're thinking that you're doing YouTube automation, unless you're rich already, bro, it's not going to work most of the time. Most of the time. Of course, there are outliers with everything, but I run everything myself for my shorts channels. It takes me about an hour a day. But I get so much more ROI than I would with a regular job. So, I'm completely fine with that. Ricking in thousands a month for an hour a day making YouTube shorts is 10 times easier than virtually any job you can think about. So, I don't want to discourage people and what I would say is this. YouTube automation is only a thing if you've made it to this super endgame of YouTube, right? Where you're raking in dozens of thousands of dollars every month and you can afford to spend big bucks, right? Just to make your life a little bit easier. But if you're not there yet, you shouldn't be worried about YouTube automation. You should be worried about you should be worried about building up your skill set and building up your channel. And that's really where you're going to get 99% of the results. Hope this video helps somebody out. If you want to use my voice, the link is in the description. If you want to win $50, use these songs in your shorts and then submit it on this Google form. Everything is in the description and the pin comment if I can remember. And I hope you guys have a great day. Peace out.",
