 the music deals to not transform the content at all. For example, when you're ripping from like movies or TV shows, people who are just taking TV show clips and then putting the playlist music deal or any other music deal to monetize copyrighted content without transforming it at all. YouTube finally had enough of that. That's not something I ever personally did. In full transparency, that's I'm pretty sure what's going on. Now, as far as I know, Playlist got a warning and all the other companies were terminated. That's just from what I know. The companies that had channels that were violating this policy, that is. So, now I want to share you guys some messages from Playlist because I don't have like a hotline to them or anything, but I've been talking to them. So, if you log into Playlist, if you had a Playlist account, if you log into the website right now, you'll get a a notice, a pop-up notice on your screen just saying your account has been identified for abusive activity, blah blah blah. I'm not going to read the whole thing, but that got sent to everybody. And basically what you're going to do if you haven't violated that copyright policy, like you haven't been ripping movies and not transforming them at all. And keep in mind what I'm saying cuz when I said this in my Discord, everybody had all these questions. If your content is transformative, you should be able to request a payout. If your content is not transformative, I mean, you can try to request a payout, but I they're not going to let it happen, I don't believe. So, right now with Playus PSA, the best thing to do if you have money in there that you want to get out, go to the website, submit the payout request, and then what's going to happen is that their team is going to review, they're going to have to go through and review manually all those channels to make sure that all the channels who requested a payout to make sure that they're not violating movie and TV show copyright, etc. Then, and this i