uction in shorts views and stuff. I have been getting cooked. Now, in the last few days, I've had some really big days, but as crazy as those days have been, they haven't made up for the lost revenue that I've had late July and August. Okay, I got cooked. And largely, I've talked about this a decent amount in my Discord in terms of having videos with great stats that didn't go viral. And people go, \"Oh, well, the stats aren't everything.\" I know, I know. But these are videos where I've been doing this game for long enough, like two years, I could kind of predict what videos would have a chance to go viral. for the last month or so, month and a half really, I've been just been getting like absolutely busted. So, luckily in the last few days, that finally picked up, but it's been a pretty big hit to my income. So, I haven't had much time to sit around and record videos for this channel because I love helping you guys out. But, first and foremost, I need to make money, survive for myself. So, I have been grinding out all day, every day, just trying to improve videos, post more, uh try different strategies, um and of course continuously learning, starting new channels, and just trying to position myself to make more money in the future because, uh for for reference, I mean, my income got like my income got slashed by like 70% for the last month. So, especially with Playlist, the music deal that I use pausing. So, that's been pretty humbling for me. Then, it's like a double gut punch because uh to be completely transparent, like the situation sucks, right? And so I sort of pride myself on giving you guys good information, right? And so even if players comes back and I like I said repeatedly, I am hopeful. But even if they come back, I still basically am responsible to some degree for promoting something that has this confusion around it and uh people are blaming me for it. And uh honestly, I don't I don't blame you guys. I I get it. And I know even in the comment secti