strating. I know it feels unfair, but that's just the way the world works, guys. It's stupid. It shouldn't exist, but all hope isn't lost because usually there is at least some way around this. But for most people, it is going to require a lot of troubleshooting. So, just be ready and prepared for that. So, what is the zero view jail exactly? For whatever reason, YouTube thinks you're a bot or is shadowbanning you. What you guys need to understand is that this isn't about your content being bad or good. This is just straight up YouTube is not giving you a chance. I have had channels before that were stuck in zero view jail and then when I looked online, everybody was saying, \"Oh, bro, just upload better content. Shadowbs aren't real.\" Then I upload them on a different channel, the exact same video. Boom. The video gets like 500,000 views. Yes, shadow bands are absolutely real. And don't listen to anybody who says they aren't. I'm going to start with some basics here, and it'll probably get more advanced as the video goes on. I want to make this video as concise as possible, but to be honest, guys, there's just so much information here that this is one of the most complicated topics when it comes to shorts. So, I don't know how long this video will be exactly. We'll see. If you guys have questions, before you type them in the comments, please watch the video all the way through because it might be answered later on in the video. Like I said, I'm going to try to make this as in-depth as I can. This video is probably going to be all over the place, but if there's one thing I can guarantee, it'll be the most comprehensive, greatest video on this topic that you'll ever see. I think that's mostly everything I need to talk about before we get into it. So, let's start this. Okay, so like I said, starting out with the basic here, conventional knowledge is to use an aged account. And for the sake of this video, I would say an aged account is anything that's like at least 6 